# Deepfathom Echo (a blue-green 4/4): "At the beginning of combat on your turn, this creature explores. Then you may have it become
# a copy of another creature you control until end of turn." Turn 1: Bot1 casts it off Black Lotus and Mox Sapphire, with a Dragon's
# Rage Channeler (1/1) and an Ornithopter (0/2) beside it. At the beginning of combat it explores first (CR 701.44a): the revealed
# Mox Emerald is not a land, so the Echo gets a +1/+1 counter and Bot1 leaves the card on top. Then Bot1 chooses the Channeler (a
# choice as it resolves, not a target): the Echo is a Dragon's Rage Channeler 1/1 with its counter, 2/2, until end of turn (CR 707.2,
# 707.4: the same object keeps its counter). On turn 3 it is the Echo again, 5/5 with the counter. It explores again at the
# next combat: the revealed Island goes to Bot1's hand and the counter is not added to. Bot1 is asked which creature to copy
# and may choose none; the Echo itself and Bot2's Ornithopter are not offered.

